TypeScript adaptation adds finite planned sample metadata, asynchronous bounded
WriteHandle writes, input packet validation, cancellation and output abort.

CLI stream selection adapts pinned fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c (map_auto_video,
map_auto_audio and disposition propagation), LGPL-2.1-or-later, plus MOV enabled
track handling from movenc.c. These files are part of FFmpeg; their upstream
notices and source remain in the pinned submodule. AAC configuration parsing
supplies codec channel counts for selection; no decoder runs in the library.

Input stream-ID parsing/matching additionally follows pinned fftools/cmdutils.c
and ordered negative mapping follows fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c.
cmdutils.c: Copyright (c)2000-2003 Fabrice Bellard, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
The TypeScript CLI keeps unsigned container IDs in metadata and applies the
pinned AVStream signed32-bit identity only when matching input ID selectors.

Language metadata tokenization follows pinned libavutil/avstring.c av_get_token:
Copyright (c)2000,2001,2002 Fabrice Bellard; (c)2007 Mans Rullgard.
LGPL-2.1-or-later. Language selector matching follows cmdutils.c.

H264 initial video-delay estimation adapts mov_estimate_video_delay from
pinned libavformat/mov.c, LGPL-2.1-or-later. Original source and notices remain
in upstream/ffmpeg/libavformat/mov.c; license text is COPYING.LGPLv2.1.
The TypeScript implementation uses bigint PTS and a bounded17entry ring.


h264-rate-probe.ts adapts ff_rfps_add_frame/ff_rfps_calculate from demux.c and
av_guess_frame_rate from avformat.c at the pinned commit, LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Copyright (c)2000,2001,2002 Fabrice Bellard. Original source/notices remain
in upstream/ffmpeg/libavformat; license text is COPYING.LGPLv2.1. The TypeScript
adaptation bounds standard-rate state to399entries and index probing to the
configured budget; general multi-stream probe termination remains unverified.

Original-file start-time adjustment before stream mapping follows
fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c and ffmpeg_opt.c (MOV does not use the TS_DISCONT
selected-stream correction) at the pinned commit above.

H264 packet DTS order checking, PTS-window selection, error scores and aging
are adapted from libavformat/demux.c compute_pkt_fields/select_from_pts_buffer
at the pinned FFmpeg commit. LGPL-2.1-or-later; source and notices remain in the
upstream submodule. The independent codec parameter inspector supplies active
SPS restrictions; packet clock probing does not load a Wasm decoder.

Copy clock probing is restricted to selected AVC video tracks. AAC backward
edit clocks retain their per-stream sequence until strict mux timestamp
normalization; they do not enter the H264 SPS probe path.

Selected audio sample-rate preflight follows pinned libavformat/mux.c
sample_rate<=0 -> AVERROR(EINVAL),with ffmpeg.c process status234. Canonical
reason is sample rate not set;the check applies to selected output tracks.
Full diagnostic formatting/Native OS side-effect compatibility is not claimed.

Conflicting -y/-n validation follows assert_file_overwrite in pinned
fftools/ffmpeg_opt.c:AVERROR(EINVAL),observed as234. The check follows source
and selected codec validation and precedes mux audio header validation.
LGPL-2.1-or-later;upstream copyright/license notices remain in the submodule.
Existing-output refusal AVERROR_EXIT/0 has a separate scoped Node/R2 contract;
full Native protocol remains unverified.

Overwrite refusal sequencing follows pinned fftools/ffmpeg_mux_init.c and
assert_file_overwrite in ffmpeg_opt.c. Native AVERROR_EXIT maps to0 in
ffmpeg.c finish;the Core ExecutionExit models this graceful non-publication.
Native OS empty-file failure effects are not reproduced by atomic VFS output.
